<title>UK: Oasis falls on profit-taking after H1.</title>
<headline>Oasis falls on profit-taking after H1.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Oasis Stores fell on profit-taking after the fashion retailer posted its interim results, traders said.</p>
<p>At 1138 GMT, the shares were down 13-1/2p to 392-1/2p. They have risen by more than 40 percent since mid-March.</p>
<p>Traders said the figures, which showed a 40 percent increase in pre-tax profits, were largely in line with expectations, but that investors took profits nonetheless.</p>
<p>&quot;It's better to travel than to arrive,&quot; said one trader.</p>
<p>--Debra Sherman, London newsroom +44 171 542 4026</p>
</text>
